server: Read another process's memory with process_vm_readv, without stopping it.

read_process_memory() PTRACE_ATTACHes the first thread of the target
process (its main thread), waits for the SIGSTOP, reads, and detaches -
for every single NtReadVirtualMemory.  Windows does not stop anything to
serve ReadProcessMemory, and a caller that reads another process thousands
of times a second (MapleStory TW's BlackCipher64 does, in bursts of a few
seconds every few seconds since the 2026-10-21 game update) keeps the
target's main thread stopped for a large part of the time.

In game, 1-second samples during a burst: BlackCipher64 at 55-65% CPU,
wineserver at 25-29%, and the game's main thread falling from ~50% to
~20%; the game stutters.  perf on wineserver during play: 22% in
suspend_for_ptrace, 15% in read_process_memory, ~24% in ptrace / wait4.
ntsync does not help (it takes the game's own waits off the server, not
this).

On Linux, try process_vm_readv() first.  It needs the same ptrace access
the old path already has, stops nothing, and is one syscall.  A short or
failed read falls back to the ptrace path unchanged, so error codes stay
the same (unmapped address and a read across the end of a mapping still
fail with ERROR_NOACCESS / got=0, measured).

Measured with a child whose main thread spins a counter while the parent
ReadProcessMemory()s 4 KB from it as fast as it can, for one second:

                        child speed vs idle   reads/s
    before              46-55%                67-73k
    after               98-99%                160k

---
--- a/server/ptrace.c
+++ b/server/ptrace.c
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/wait.h>
+#ifdef __linux__
+# include <sys/uio.h>
+#endif
 #ifdef HAVE_SYS_PTRACE_H
 # include <sys/ptrace.h>
 #endif
@@ -355,6 +358,16 @@
         return 0;
     }
 
+#ifdef __linux__
+    /* no need to stop a thread of the target: try a direct copy first,
+     * and only fall back to ptrace if it does not read everything */
+    if (process->unix_pid != -1)
+    {
+        struct iovec local = { dest, size }, remote = { (void *)(unsigned long)ptr, size };
+        if (process_vm_readv( process->unix_pid, &local, 1, &remote, 1, 0 ) == size) return 1;
+    }
+#endif
+
     first_offset = ptr % sizeof(long);
     last_offset = (size + first_offset) % sizeof(long);
     if (!last_offset) last_offset = sizeof(long);
